WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.290
You're making a steel
display frame for a shop.

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:03.980
They've just called to let you know

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.670
they want to fill more of the window.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:07.810
Could you make the frame a metre longer?

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.530
What does that do to the price?

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.800
Originally, you would open
the drawing in Onshape,

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.570
where your engineer designs the frame.

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:16.030
You'd compare the two versions

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:18.360
and write down the length of all four rails.

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:20.380
Then you'd open bexio,

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:21.980
where you keep your material prices.

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:24.716
Six-metre bars cost forty-eight francs.

00:00:24.716 --> 00:00:26.120
Twelve-metre bars are ninety-six.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:28.340
Now comes the fiddly bit.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:30.460
Four short bars would do the job.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.210
But could you buy less steel

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:33.720
if you used a longer bar?

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:35.580
You'd have to sketch out the cuts.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.220
With a custom portal from Reed Solutions,

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.000
those checks happen automatically.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:42.000
You sign in to your workshop.

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:43.660
All your projects are here.

00:00:43.830 --> 00:00:45.720
You can see the shelves,
the counter brackets,

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:47.160
and the shop's display frame.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:50.510
Open the frame project
and all its drawings are here.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.030
When your engineer saved
this version in Onshape,

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.470
the portal automatically reread the CAD file.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.050
It found that all four
rails were a metre longer.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:00:59.180
Here's the original

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:01.230
and the drawings for the individual parts.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:04.720
The portal has already
checked both prices in bexio,

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.320
worked out which bars to buy,

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:07.590
and updated the job price

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:09.330
from two hundred and seventy francs

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:10.220
to three hundred and thirty.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:11.880
Here's why.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:14.500
The original rails were
just under three metres.

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:15.860
Two fitted on a bar,

00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:17.960
so two bars gave you all four rails.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:20.770
Now each rail is just under four metres.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.490
Only one fits on each six-metre bar.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.350
So what about the longer stock?

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.170
Three rails fit on one twelve-metre bar.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.090
One short bar covers the fourth.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.830
That's forty-eight francs
more steel than before.

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:35.130
The estimate keeps the two hours of labour

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:36.730
and the twenty-five per cent markup

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:37.720
you'd already allowed.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.080
You can adjust either
before you agree the price.

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:42.580
Once you're happy, finalise this version.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:43.840
When the work is done,

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:44.970
one click in the portal

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.840
creates the draft invoice
in bexio, ready for review.

00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:52.070
When the shop asks why the extra
metre costs sixty francs,

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:54.300
you can show them exactly what changed.

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:57.550
Export the revised drawing,
the cutting plan and the price

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.440
straight from the portal,
together in one PDF.
